--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS (read end-to-end — covenant #3)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TeslaFeatureFlagsPage.tsx is a dedicated page wrapper that promotes the Tesla "Feature Flags"
surface to a first-class route: `PageContainer(title=t('featureConfig.title'), subtitle=
t('featureConfig.subtitle'))` hosting the shared `<FeatureToggles/>` component. FeatureToggles
(features/settings/components/FeatureToggles.tsx) renders the GlassPanel header (Flag IconBox +
title + subtitle + "Synced …" + Refresh button) and the feature table / EmptyState. The page's
own parity surface is exactly the two PageContainer strings; the embedded component is a SEPARATE,
already-shipped P3 parity unit. On the web the title/subtitle appear BOTH in the page chrome AND in
the component header — the native page reproduces that faithfully (it is not a bug to "dedupe").

The native FeatureToggles component already exists at full parity (P3):
  TeslaSync/feature-views/FeatureToggles{,.Model,.Adapter,.Views,.Previews,.Tests}.swift
  — a `FeatureTogglesModel(source:telemetry:toast:)` that renders loading/empty/error/content/stale/
  offline. This P7 page is the wrapper that hosts it at /tesla-features (it does NOT re-implement it).

