OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`. That path does
NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's real, compiled canonical
admin-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — where all five sibling P7 admin pages ship
(ApiPlayground / DiskForecast / FleetTelemetryCoverage / LiveSignalInspector / SchemaDrift) and which
`Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path. The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`, the faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Admin`.
This is the identical reconciliation the peer ApiPlayground / DiskForecast logs recorded.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the dedicated top-level path `/tesla-features` (like `/api-playground`
→ `.apiPlayground`). A new `AppRoute.teslaFeatures` case is added (pathSegment "tesla-features";
systemImage "flag.fill" — matching the web `Flag` icon + the existing `Layout.Nav` catalog entry;
group `.account` — matching the web sidebar "Account" section where /tesla-features lives).
`AppRouteParser` auto-resolves "/tesla-features" → .teslaFeatures via pathSegment.
`TeslaFeatureFlagsRouteRegistration` hosts the page on .teslaFeatures and is chained into the
TeslaSyncApp `\.routeHosts` registry. RouteTests asserts the deep link. Recorded here per covenant #9.

